 "answer": "In the LlamaIndex node parser documentation, the basic example for using a `SentenceSplitter` specifies a `chunk_size` of 1024 and a `chunk_overlap` of 20. This is evident from the context provided in multiple parts of the documentation:\n\n1. In the context related to \"Node Parser / Text Splitter,\" the basic example sets `chunk_size=1024` and `chunk_overlap=20`:\n\n   ```python\n   node_parser = SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=1024, chunk_overlap=20)\n   ```\n\n2. Similarly, in the \"Index Usage\" section, the `SentenceSplitter` is configured with `chunk_size=1024` and `chunk_overlap=20`:\n\n   ```python\n   Settings.text_splitter = SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=1024, chunk_overlap=20)\n   ```\n\n3. In the \"High-Level Transformation API\" section, the same settings are applied:\n\n   ```python\n   index = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(\n       documents,\n       transformations=[SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=1024, chunk_overlap=20)],\n   )\n   ```\n\nThese instances consistently use a `chunk_size` of 1024 and a `chunk_overlap` of 20 in their examples.",
